  "query_preview": "Outlook\nA transition in the synoptic pattern is anticipated this \nweekend as the upper ridge axis retrogrades toward the central \nGreat Plains, amplifying as an upper trough digs across the \nCanadian Maritimes and New England forming an Omega Block. This\nwill shift central Illinois into a northwest flow regime by \nearly this weekend. An 850mb baroclinic zone will straddle the \nregion, with a backdoor cold front providing a modest cooling \ntrend in northeast Illinois; temperatures will drop from the 90s\ninto the mid-to- upper 80s Sunday and Monday for parts of the \narea that see frontal passage. Further south, an Extreme Heat \nWarning remains in effect. This reprieve in our northeast \ncounties will be short-lived, however, as the ridge axis builds \nback east early next week, supporting a return of widespread \n90-degree heat by Tuesday and Wednesday.",
